{"seq":7,"slug":"soft-systems-methodology","title":"软系统方法论","stage":"DONE","category":"systems-thinking","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology","rating":{"composite":3.61,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.8,"coverage":3,"positioning":null,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"软系统方法论-总览\">软系统方法论·总览</h1><p>把一台水泵装错了，工程师能算出哪里不对；可是「这家医院该如何分诊」「这个团队为什么协作不畅」这类问题，连「问题到底是什么」都没人说得清——不同的人站在不同立场，看到的根本是不同的麻烦。Peter Checkland 在兰卡斯特大学用十余年实践，正是为了对付后面这一类<strong>结构不良的人类活动系统</strong>：目标含混、利益分歧、价值观打架。软系统方法论（Soft Systems Methodology, SSM）由此诞生，它不假设有一个客观待解的「问题」，而把「系统」当成帮助人们学习、辩论、达成共识的思考工具。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 沿四条主线层层递进。<strong>基础</strong>先讲清软硬之分：硬系统方法把「系统」当作世界里真实存在、目标既定的对象去优化；软系统方法把「系统」当作我们脑中用来理解混乱现实的认识装置——这一转向的关键，是承认每个人都带着自己的**世界观（Weltanschauung）**在看问题。<strong>核心方法</strong>给出三件趁手工具：丰富图把混乱情境画成一张图，根定义与 CATWOE 把「我们要谈的是什么系统」精确说清，概念模型再从根定义推出「这样一个系统应当包含哪些活动」。<strong>探究循环</strong>把工具串成一套学习流程：经典的七阶段过程、把概念模型与现实对比并展开辩论、最终筛出既「系统上合意」又「文化上可行」的变革。<strong>实践</strong>回到现实：Checkland 1990 年提出的模式1与模式2如何在咨询与日常中切换，SSM 与硬系统工程、系统动力学、Ackoff 交互规划、批判系统思考等方法的分工，以及医疗、信息系统、组织变革中的真实案例。</p>\n<p>四条线不是并列罗列，而是一条由「认识论」走向「操作」再走向「落地」的路径：先理解为什么需要软方法，再学会三件工具，再把工具组织成探究循环，最后在真实组织里运用。</p>\n<p><strong>本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工</strong>：<a href=\"../systems-thinking-fundamentals/system-concepts/what-is-a-system\">系统思维基础</a> 讲「系统」的一般概念、反馈回路与心智模型，是所有系统思维的入门地基；本 hub 不重复这些基础，而专注于 Checkland 这一<strong>特定方法论</strong>。<a href=\"../cybernetics/second-order-cybernetics/constructivism\">控制论</a> 的二阶控制论与建构主义为「观察者塑造所见」提供哲学根基，本 hub 借用其结论但不展开其数学。<a href=\"../systems-practice/organizational-systems/org-as-system\">系统实践</a> 讲组织、社会、软件作为系统的广义实践，本 hub 是其中一种可落地的具体方法——遇到组织层面的通用议题，请去那里。</p>\n<p><strong>推荐学习路径</strong>。初学者：按章顺序读完即可，先建立软硬之辨的直觉，再学三件工具，不必一上来就背 CATWOE。有系统思维背景的实践者：可先读「核心方法」与「探究循环」两章直接上手，「基础」当作回顾。咨询/分析师：重点在「实践」章的模式1/模式2与案例，结合工具章按需查阅。</p>\n<p><strong>前置知识</strong>：了解「系统」「边界」「反馈」等基本概念会让阅读顺畅，若陌生，建议先过一遍 <a href=\"../systems-thinking-fundamentals/system-concepts/what-is-a-system\">什么是系统</a>。无需任何数学或编程基础，SSM 本质是一种结构化的思考与对话方式。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"hard-vs-soft-systems","title":"硬系统与软系统","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/foundations/hard-vs-soft-systems"},{"seq":2,"slug":"checkland-ssm-origins","title":"Checkland 与 SSM 起源","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/foundations/checkland-ssm-origins"},{"seq":3,"slug":"worldview-weltanschauung","title":"世界观与多元视角","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/foundations/worldview-weltanschauung"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"core-method","title":"核心方法","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/core-method","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"rich-pictures","title":"丰富图","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/core-method/rich-pictures"},{"seq":2,"slug":"root-definitions-catwoe","title":"根定义与 CATWOE","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/core-method/root-definitions-catwoe"},{"seq":3,"slug":"conceptual-models","title":"概念模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/core-method/conceptual-models"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"inquiry-cycle","title":"探究循环","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/inquiry-cycle","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"seven-stage-process","title":"七阶段探究过程","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/inquiry-cycle/seven-stage-process"},{"seq":2,"slug":"comparison-debate","title":"对比与辩论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/inquiry-cycle/comparison-debate"},{"seq":3,"slug":"feasible-desirable-change","title":"可行且合意的变革","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/inquiry-cycle/feasible-desirable-change"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"mode1-mode2-use","title":"模式1与模式2运用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/practice/mode1-mode2-use"},{"seq":2,"slug":"ssm-vs-other-methods","title":"与其它方法论的关系","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/practice/ssm-vs-other-methods"},{"seq":3,"slug":"case-studies-applications","title":"案例与应用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/systems-thinking/soft-systems-methodology/practice/case-studies-applications"}]}]}